WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:06.019
In this section, we will explore how version control is handled in the engine, starting

2
00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:09.279
with the latest version of Unreal Engine.

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:13.300
Unreal Engine allows users to directly connect to their fully integrated version control

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.760
solution by navigating to the Tools pull-down menu in the main menu and then navigating

5
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.320
through to the Revision Control section.

6
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.260
Here you will be able to select the Connect to Revision Control option, and that will

7
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:32.539
bring up a pop-up menu allowing you to select your Revision Control provider.

8
00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:39.310
In addition to Perforce, Unreal Engine supports Subversion, Git, and PlasticCSM.

9
00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.350
Once the provider is selected, users can input their Revision Control server, username,

10
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.679
and workspace.

11
00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:52.200
If established in the Unreal Engine Settings, users can automatically connect by enabling

12
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.539
the established P4 config.

13
00:00:55.539 --> 00:01:00.460
Once you've made a successful connection, Unreal Engine will notify you with a pop-up

14
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.729
in the lower right-hand corner.

15
00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:07.209
Additionally, the Quick Access menu for Revision Control is located in the lower

16
00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:11.810
right-hand corner of any active window in Unreal Engine.

17
00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:16.390
This Quick Access Revision Control menu will also allow users to make any changes

18
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.709
to the Revision Control settings, modify files, or utilize any of the version control

19
00:01:21.709 --> 00:01:25.209
options from the Action menu.

20
00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:29.569
The Revision Control menu options will change depending on the state of your checked

21
00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:35.209
asset, and additional options will become active or inactive depending on your Version

22
00:01:35.209 --> 00:01:37.140
Control provider.

23
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.340
The most commonly used menu actions are going to be Checkout, Mark for Add, Check

24
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.760
In, and Revert.

25
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.019
When making changes to assets, maps, or pretty much anything within your Unreal Engine project,

26
00:01:50.019 --> 00:01:53.959
you will need to start by checking out the files that you want to modify.

27
00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:58.120
To do that, you simply need to right-click on the asset, go to the Revision Control

28
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.700
options, and check out those files directly.

29
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.480
Once you've checked out a file, you will note that the file itself will have

30
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.219
an icon appear in the lower right-hand corner.

31
00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:15.639
This red Check Mark icon shows that the file has been checked out for modification.

32
00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:20.620
Additionally, as you go through your Version Control, you're going to find a few different

33
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:26.500
icons that identify the state of any new or checked out file that needs to be submitted

34
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.020
with Version Control active.

35
00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.500
So any time a file is changed, it must be checked out of Version Control either

36
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.900
directly or as part of a mass checkout through the Quick Access Revision Control

37
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.080
menus in the lower right-hand corner.

38
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.759
This will allow any modified files to be checked out prior to saving.

39
00:02:45.759 --> 00:02:50.000
So if you're working on a level, and you notice that little asterisk, then that

40
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.599
file needs to be saved.

41
00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:57.400
But so too would any sublevels need to be saved, and while you might not see the asterisks

42
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:03.599
for those sublevels, the Check Out Modified Files option won't miss them.

43
00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.159
When you are ready to run through the Check Out Modified Files option, it will automatically

44
00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:13.159
open a pop-up menu that will allow you to select those files for modification and

45
00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:17.560
add the red Check Mark indicator to those files just like we talked about in the last

46
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.610
slide.

47
00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.009
Once you are finished making all of your modifications, you are ready to submit your

48
00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:26.050
changes to the Version Control system.

49
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:30.129
When files need to be checked back in to your Version Control provider, simply go back

50
00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:34.530
to that Quick Access Revision Control menu in the lower right-hand corner to submit

51
00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.469
your saved content.

52
00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:39.949
This will bring up a Submit Files pop-up menu.

53
00:03:39.949 --> 00:03:46.229
From there, check the assets you wish to submit or verify that they are already checked

54
00:03:46.229 --> 00:03:51.580
and then fill out the change list much like you did when working inside Perforce directly.

55
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.699
Additionally, you have the option to keep files checked out if you want to continue

56
00:03:55.699 --> 00:03:58.580
working on them after you've made the submission.

57
00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.439
Once you click the Submit button, the submission will process and you will receive

58
00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:08.060
another pop-up notifier in the bottom right-hand corner of the engine that says the submission

59
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.060
is successful and it will provide you a new change list number.

60
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.620
Verify that change list number from the pop-up notification with the Version Control history

61
00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.980
inside your Version Control provider after the submission is complete.

62
00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.620
Alright, that's it for this section.

63
00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.819
In our next section, we will look at how Unreal Engine for Fortnite handles Version

64
00:04:28.819 --> 00:04:29.319
Control.
